@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Delete a second task while a toast is visible
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (UI components)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TodoItemComponent" as item
  participant "ToastComponent" as toast
end box
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (state and API client)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TodoStore" as store
  participant "HttpTodoApi" as api
end box
box "Backend — Laravel API (HTTP layer)" #D1FADF
  participant "TodoController" as ctrl
end box
note over store : Task A deleted earlier, toast "Task deleted" shows Undo for task A
user -> item : Click the delete control on task B (L2-015)
item -> store : delete(idB) through TodoPageComponent
store -> store : Remove row B, keep todo B and its position (L2-015)
store -> store : Replace the toast value, Undo target is now task B only (L2-015)
store --> toast : Toast updated to the latest deletion
store -> store : Restart the 6 s timer at the full duration
store -> api : delete(idB)
api -> ctrl : DELETE /api/v1/todos/{idB}
ctrl --> api : 204 No Content
api --> store : Delete confirmed
note over store, toast : Task A can no longer be restored from the UI, its deletion stands (L2-015)
@enduml
